{
  "mn58:0.1": "Middle Discourses 58 ",
  "mn58:0.2": "With Prince Abhaya ",
  "mn58:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn58:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn58:2.1": "Then Prince Abhaya went up to the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Jain Ñātika said to him, ",
  "mn58:3.1": "“Come, prince, refute the ascetic Gotama’s doctrine. ",
  "mn58:3.2": "Then you will get a good reputation: ",
  "mn58:3.3": "‘Prince Abhaya refuted the doctrine of the ascetic Gotama, so mighty and powerful!’” ",
  "mn58:3.4": "“But sir, how am I to do this?” ",
  "mn58:3.5": "“Here, prince, go to the ascetic Gotama and say to him: ",
  "mn58:3.6": "‘Sir, may the Realized One utter speech that is disliked by others?’ ",
  "mn58:3.7": "When he’s asked this, if he answers: ",
  "mn58:3.8": "‘He may, prince,’ say this to him, ",
  "mn58:3.9": "‘So what then, sir, is the difference between you and an ordinary person? ",
  "mn58:3.10": "For even an ordinary person may utter speech that is disliked by others.’ ",
  "mn58:3.11": "But if he answers, ",
  "mn58:3.12": "‘He may not, prince,’ say this to him: ",
  "mn58:3.13": "‘So why then, sir, did you declare of Devadatta: ",
  "mn58:3.14": "“Devadatta is going to a place of loss, to hell, there to remain for an eon, irredeemable”? ",
  "mn58:3.15": "Devadatta was angry and upset with what you said.’ ",
  "mn58:3.16": "When you put t